======================================================================
PART 4: Quotient walk proof approach for n=14
======================================================================

INITIAL SEGMENT PROOF:
  At t=1/14: positions = {k/14 : k=0,...,13}
  Distances: min_k ||k/14|| = 1/14 = threshold
  This is a BOUNDARY lonely time (wall). QED for initial segment.

INDEPENDENCE MODEL:
  If all 7 CRT classes were independent:
    P(all safe) ≈ (6/7)^7 = 0.3399 = 34.0%
  This would give a LARGE lonely measure.
  The actual lonely measure is MUCH smaller (often wall-only)
  because the classes are NOT independent — they're correlated
  through the shared time parameter t.

PROOF TARGET:
  Show: for any primitive {v_1,...,v_13}, the set
    L = {t : all ||v_i t|| >= 1/14} is nonempty.

  EQUIVALENT (via CRT 14=2×7):
    L = intersection of 7 sets, one per CRT class.
    Each class-safe set has measure >= (6/7)^2 ≈ 73.5% (for coprime pairs)
    or 6/7 ≈ 85.7% (for the singleton class).

  The intersection is empty only if the 7 class-safe sets are
  'perfectly anti-correlated' — covering each other's holes exactly.
  The metagraph walk structure should prevent this.

